Two changes on top of MastaG/bc250-dual-audio, made on 2026-09-11 after the
package took over the only audio device on the dev board:

1. 90-bc250-audio-mode.lua: an encoded output (AC-3) is never entered on an
   automatic fallback. With the display in standby the native HDMI sink is
   missing, WirePlumber falls back to the always-present AC-3 frontend, and a
   monitor with speakers then plays the raw bitstream as PCM: a loud noise.
   Only an explicit choice (default.configured.audio.sink, i.e. the user
   picking "Dolby Digital 5.1 (AC3)" in the settings) may take the hardware.
2. 60-bc250-ac3-output.conf: priority.session of the encoded frontends
   lowered from 100/90 to 10/9, so a real sink always wins the automatic
   default when it exists.

Proven on the dev board with the AC-3 path pointed at null: native wins on a
fresh state, removing the native sink logs "automatic fallback landed on
bc250_ac3; ignored" and creates no backend, the native sink is taken back as
soon as it returns.
